{
  "$comment": "The accessibility contract as data, in the shape samourai-visio/scripts/check-contrast.py already consumes. `fg` and `bg` are token paths from tokens.json, or a literal #hex. `min` is 4.5 for text (WCAG 2.1 SC 1.4.3) or 3.0 for a non-text boundary, control edge or focus indicator (SC 1.4.11); the large-text 3:1 exemption is not used anywhere in this system. `fgAlpha` composites the foreground over the background before measuring — a translucent colour measured as if it were opaque reports a ratio no user ever sees. `exempt` records a row that is measured and reported but not gated. `expect: \"fail\"` inverts the row: it is a pair the design system forbids, and the gate fails if it ever starts passing, because that means the palette moved under the rule.",
